# Unadjusted positions: position_identity

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for
[`position_identity()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/position_identity.html) has no
examples, so this notebook says only what the page describes and where Giggly stands.

`position_identity()` adjusts nothing: every row is drawn where its position aesthetics put it,
whether or not its mark overlaps another. Giggly has it as `position: :identity`, which every
layer function with a `position:` option takes, and the default of most:
`Giggly.Plot.geom_point/3` draws each point at its row's `x` and `y`, unadjusted, as ggplot2's
`geom_point()` does by default. `Giggly.Plot.geom_bar/3` and `Giggly.Plot.geom_col/3` stack by
default, and with `position: :identity` draw bars over one another, as `position = "identity"`
does.
